From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <bap@debian.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:19:02 +0000
Subject: Allow QLOGO_VERSION to be set on the cmake command line

Forwarded: no

The QLOGOVERSION Logo variable is taken from "git describe", which
yields "unknown" when building from a tarball and an unrelated
packaging tag when building inside a packaging git repository.  Allow
the builder to set it explicitly with -DQLOGO_VERSION=...
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 16 +++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index dd5916f..ebdfa5e 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -35,13 +35,15 @@ if(NOT QLOGO_CSLS_FILES)
     message(FATAL_ERROR "No CSLS files found in ${QLOGO_CSLS_SRC}")
 endif()
 
-execute_process(
-    COMMAND git describe --tags
-    WORKING_DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}
-    OUTPUT_VARIABLE QLOGO_VERSION
-    OUTPUT_STRIP_TRAILING_WHITESPACE
-    ERROR_QUIET
-)
+if(NOT QLOGO_VERSION)
+    execute_process(
+        COMMAND git describe --tags
+        WORKING_DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}
+        OUTPUT_VARIABLE QLOGO_VERSION
+        OUTPUT_STRIP_TRAILING_WHITESPACE
+        ERROR_QUIET
+    )
+endif()
 if(NOT QLOGO_VERSION)
     set(QLOGO_VERSION "unknown")
 endif()
